+// CRYPTO_fork_detect_bump_generation tells BoringSSL that the address space
+// was duplicated by a mechanism it cannot observe, for example a VM snapshot
+// that was restored into several clones. It advances the fork generation, so
+// every thread reseeds its PRNG state from the operating system before the
+// output of its next `RAND_bytes` call that begins after this function returns.
+// A call already in progress on another thread completes with its old state.
+// It is safe to call while other threads use BoringSSL.
+//
+// On platforms where fork detection is unavailable (the generation is zero),
+// BoringSSL already draws OS entropy on every call and this function does
+// nothing.
+//
+// WARNING: This function affects BoringSSL for the entire address space. Only
+// code with global knowledge of the application should call it, directly
+// after the duplication it knows about.
+OPENSSL_EXPORT void CRYPTO_fork_detect_bump_generation(void);
+
